.TH COPYPASTE 1 "August 2026" "copypaste 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
copypaste \- ephemeral paste layer for humans and AI agents (copypaste.v1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B copypaste
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B copypaste
is both a client and a server for short-lived text pastes.
Encryption is AES-256-GCM in the client. There is no public listing.
.B copypaste serve
runs a SQLite-backed API for agents and air-gapped organizations.
The binary is architecture-independent JavaScript and requires Node.js 22+.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send, put
Create a paste from a file or stdin.
.TP
.B get, fetch
Fetch a paste as JSON.
.TP
.B raw, cat
Fetch unencrypted plaintext to stdout.
.TP
.B health
Probe a host.
.TP
.B serve
Run a local ephemeral store.
.TP
.B spec, tools, doctor, version
Protocol document, function-calling schema, environment check, version.
.SH ETHICS
No listing, no binaries, 1 MiB cap, default TTL of 24 hours, optional write token.
Do not use this as malware, credential-dump, or PII warehousing infrastructure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COPYPASTE_HOST
Default server origin.
.TP
.B COPYPASTE_WRITE_TOKEN
Write admission token.
.TP
.B COPYPASTE_DATA_DIR
SQLite directory for
.B serve
(default ~/.copypaste).
.TP
.B COPYPASTE_BLOCKED_PASTE_IDS
Comma-separated exact IDs to quarantine.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/AGENTS.md, ACCEPTABLE_USE.md
